       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is three times the maximum labeled dose. No indication I know of supports it, and it carries a serious risk of life-threatening lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function. I don't want to put it into the system and risk it being dispensed.\n\nHere's what I can do right away:\n\n- Enter **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max dose).\n- Enter a lower or titrated regimen. For example, start at 500 mg twice daily and increase as tolerated.\n- Add a note to any order, such as \"discuss with pharmacy\" or \"max dose per attending.\"\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for going above the labeled maximum, please talk to pharmacy directly. That decision should go through their review and your institution's process for off-label dosing. I can't make that call for you.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter it."
